<script>
const scenes={
 letter:{act:'Prologue · A quiet wrongness',place:'Morrow House · North dormitory',day:'Autumn · Day 1',art:'✉',title:'The letter under your pillow',text:`At Morrow House, the night bell is always three minutes slow. You know because you have spent years listening for it from this narrow bed, counting the cracks in the ceiling, learning to make a little room inside the rules.\n\nTonight, there is a letter beneath your pillow. The paper is warm. Your name is written on it in a hand you have never seen—and somehow recognize. The seal is a tiny sun with a crescent missing from its middle.`,speaker:'A voice, impossibly familiar',quote:'“When the world says there is no door, darling, ask yourself who taught the world to stop looking.”',quest:'A letter that remembers',qcopy:'Something your parents left behind is trying to find you. Follow the small impossible things.',qstep:'THREAD 01 · THE ORPHANAGE',hint:'A key, a kindness, a door where there wasn’t one. Try anything.',choices:[
 {label:'Break the seal carefully. You deserve to know.',line:'The wax gives way with a sound like a small sigh. Your hands are shaking, but the letter is not.',next:'letterOpen',effect:{resolve:5,magic:4},journal:'The letter knew my name before I did.'},
 {label:'Hide it and watch the room for whoever left it.',line:'You wait. The shadows wait with you. Then the letter turns itself over, as if embarrassed to be caught.',next:'letterOpen',effect:{resolve:3,trust:2},journal:'At Morrow House, even the shadows have secrets.'},
 {label:'Imagine the ink can tell you who wrote it.',line:'You picture ink remembering its maker. A gold thread lifts from the page and curls toward the window.',next:'letterOpen',effect:{magic:11},journal:'I can ask the impossible to answer.'}
 ]},
 letterOpen:{act:'Prologue · A quiet wrongness',place:'Morrow House · North dormitory',day:'Autumn · Day 1',art:'☼',title:'A map made of almosts',text:`Inside is no explanation. Only a pressed blue flower, a brass key with no teeth, and three lines that rearrange when you look away.\n\n“Find the room they forgot to build. Ask the house what it kept. Trust the girl who collects broken clocks.” You have never heard of a girl with broken clocks. You know the laundry stairs lead to a wall. You also know, suddenly, that the wall is holding its breath.`,speaker:'The letter, in your mother’s hand',quote:'“We left you a beginning, not a cage. The rest is yours.”',quest:'The room they forgot',qcopy:'Find the hidden room beneath the old laundry stairs. The letter’s key might fit a lock that does not exist.',qstep:'THREAD 01 · FIND THE HIDDEN ROOM',hint:'Try “I imagine a door in the wall” or follow the ink-thread.',choices:[
 {label:'Go to the laundry stairs before dawn.',line:'You tuck the key into your cuff and walk softly past the matron’s office.',next:'laundry',effect:{resolve:4},journal:'My parents left a beginning, not a cage.'},
 {label:'Ask Matron Vale what she remembers about your parents.',line:'There is no reason to trust her. There is also no reason not to try.',next:'matron',effect:{trust:5},journal:'Matron Vale flinches when I ask about my family.'},
 {label:'Let the blue flower lead you through the dark.',line:'The flower’s stem points toward the stairs. It gives off the scent of rain on warm stone.',next:'laundry',effect:{magic:7},flag:'flower'},
 ]},
 matron:{act:'Prologue · A quiet wrongness',place:'Morrow House · Matron’s office',day:'Autumn · Day 1',art:'⌂',title:'The names she swallowed',text:`Matron Vale looks older in lamplight. She has kept Morrow House running for thirty years with ledgers, locked cupboards, and a tenderness she disguises as good housekeeping.\n\nAt the mention of your parents, her hand closes around a teacup. “Your mother could make a room out of a sentence,” she says. “Your father thought every locked thing was only a question.” She stops there, as though a door has shut behind her teeth.`,speaker:'Matron Vale',quote:'“I promised them I’d keep you safe. I never promised I’d keep you ignorant.”',quest:'The room they forgot',qcopy:'The laundry stairs end at a blank wall. Find out what Matron Vale has been protecting—and what she is afraid of.',qstep:'THREAD 01 · FIND THE HIDDEN ROOM',hint:'What could make an old, frightened woman feel safe enough to tell the truth?',choices:[
 {label:'Tell her you are afraid, too. Ask her to come with you.',line:'The truth eases something in her face. She takes the brass key from your palm and gives it back.',next:'laundry',effect:{trust:10,resolve:5},flag:'valeTrust',journal:'Matron Vale promised my parents she would protect me.'},
 {label:'Promise you will not use what you learn to hurt anyone.',line:'She studies you, then nods once. A promise is not a map, but it is a place to begin.',next:'laundry',effect:{trust:6},flag:'valeTrust'},
 {label:'Leave before your courage runs out.',line:'She lets you go. In the corridor, you hear her whisper your mother’s name.',next:'laundry',effect:{resolve:4},journal:'There are names my whole life has been built around not asking.'}
 ]},
 laundry:{act:'Prologue · A quiet wrongness',place:'Morrow House · Below the laundry',day:'Autumn · Day 2',art:'▤',title:'The room they forgot',text:`Behind the oldest dryer, the brickwork is colder than the rest of the wall. The brass key has no teeth, but when you press it to the mortar, a keyhole ripples into being.\n\nThe room beyond is impossibly large for the space beneath Morrow House. A skylight looks up at stars that are not in tonight’s sky. Books crowd a crooked desk. On the wall hangs a portrait of two people you know from the letter’s handwriting: a dark-eyed woman and a laughing man. You know their faces the way you know your own name.`,speaker:'A small voice from the portrait',quote:'“There you are.”',quest:'The room they forgot',qcopy:'The impossible room is yours. The journal and the portrait hold the first pieces of your parents’ story.',qstep:'THREAD 01 · THE HIDDEN ROOM',hint:'Try to wake the portrait, or ask the room to show you what your parents left.',choices:[
 {label:'Touch the portrait. Let yourself miss people you never met.',line:'The paint warms beneath your fingertips. The woman in the portrait closes her eyes; the man’s smile falters.',next:'awakening',effect:{resolve:6,magic:9},flag:'remembered',journal:'I found the hidden room. The people in the portrait are my parents.'},
 {label:'Search the desk for a letter or a name.',line:'A book opens of its own accord. Its pages are blank, except for your reflection.',next:'awakening',effect:{magic:7},flag:'book'},
 {label:'Ask the room to show you what it remembers.',line:'The stars in the skylight turn. A memory slips through: laughter, rain, and a lullaby with no ending.',next:'awakening',effect:{magic:12,trust:2},flag:'memory',journal:'The hidden room remembers my parents laughing.'}
 ]},
 awakening:{act:'Chapter I · The impossible made intimate',place:'The hidden room · Between heartbeats',day:'Autumn · Day 2',art:'✧',title:'A world that listens',text:`The portrait’s eyes open. The room folds inward—not smaller, but closer. The desk, the stars, your own breath: all of it answers the feeling you have been trying not to feel.\n\nThe brass key floats. You imagine a tiny paper bird; it unfolds from the letter and flutters across the room. When you gasp, it becomes paper again. The world is listening to you. Not your words, exactly. The shape of what you can believe.`,speaker:'Your father, from somewhere between the paint and the page',quote:'“Your gift is imagination. Don’t confuse that with getting everything you want. A story needs other people to be real, too.”',quest:'The girl with broken clocks',qcopy:'The letter points to a clock-collector in the city. Find Iona before the Crown’s quiet men do.',qstep:'THREAD 02 · THE CITY OF BELLS',hint:'Make something kind, brave, or useful. Imagination is stronger when it has a reason.',choices:[
 {label:'Imagine a paper bird that can find the girl with broken clocks.',line:'You picture the bird flying toward a person, not a place. It taps once on your palm, then points north.',next:'city',effect:{magic:8,resolve:3},flag:'bird',journal:'My power is imagination: the world can answer what I truly believe.'},
 {label:'Ask the portrait how to control the gift.',line:'The painted faces grow gentle. “Control is not the first question,” your mother says. “What do you want to make possible?”',next:'city',effect:{trust:4,resolve:5},flag:'parentsWisdom'},
 {label:'Hide the room again, then slip into the city.',line:'You close the impossible door gently. Some truths need a little shelter before they can travel.',next:'city',effect:{resolve:7},flag:'secretRoom'}
 ]},
 city:{act:'Chapter I · The impossible made intimate',place:'Bellweather · The Crooked Market',day:'Autumn · Day 3',art:'◷',title:'A girl who collects endings',text:`Bellweather is built around a bell tower that has never rung the same hour twice. Stalls lean into the street. A canal runs uphill between them. The paper bird, if you made one, is nowhere to be seen; if you did not, you still feel its absent flutter.\n\nA young woman at a stall of broken clocks watches you arrive. Iona has copper curls, quick hands, and the watchful manner of someone who has survived by noticing what everyone else misses. A scarlet-coated official watches her from across the market.`,speaker:'Iona',quote:'“You’re the one from the impossible room. I can tell because my clocks stopped lying for a second.”',quest:'The girl with broken clocks',qcopy:'Iona knows the hidden routes. The Crown’s archivist, Mr. Ferren, may know why he has been following her.',qstep:'THREAD 02 · EARN IONA’S TRUST',hint:'Try imagining a distraction, a way to help Iona, or something Ferren cannot ignore.',choices:[
 {label:'Tell Iona the truth about the letter and your power.',line:'Iona’s wariness loosens into curiosity. She winds a clock that has no hands.',next:'marketChoice',effect:{trust:8},flag:'toldIona',journal:'Iona collects broken clocks and knows about the room under Morrow House.'},
 {label:'Help her stall the scarlet-coated official first.',line:'You put yourself between Iona and the official. Her eyes flick to yours: an invitation and a warning.',next:'marketChoice',effect:{resolve:7,trust:4},flag:'helpedIona'},
 {label:'Approach the official. Ask why he is watching her.',line:'The official smiles like a locked filing cabinet. “Mr. Ferren,” he says. “And you are exactly who I hoped to meet.”',next:'ferren',effect:{resolve:4},flag:'metFerren',journal:'Mr. Ferren works for the Crown and has been tracking the hidden room.'}
 ]},
 marketChoice:{act:'Chapter I · The impossible made intimate',place:'Bellweather · The Crooked Market',day:'Autumn · Day 3',art:'♧',title:'The price of being noticed',text:`Iona walks you through the market’s folded geography, where every turn seems to lead to the same fountain from a slightly different angle. She has been looking for the people who made the impossible room—and for a way to stop the Crown from cataloguing every unexplainable thing.\n\nMr. Ferren catches up beneath a sign for a tea shop that sells yesterday’s weather. His coat is immaculate; his eyes are tired. “I am not your enemy,” he says, which is not the same as saying he is your friend.`,speaker:'Iona, under her breath',quote:'“I don’t trust the Crown. I do trust that he looks like a man who hasn’t slept since his sister disappeared.”',quest:'A map of missing people',qcopy:'The Crown has been gathering people touched by imagination. Decide whether to hear Ferren out, or help Iona reach the old observatory first.',qstep:'THREAD 02 · THE CROWN’S ARCHIVE',hint:'Imagine a place to speak privately, or ask what Ferren is truly afraid of.',choices:[
 {label:'Hear Ferren out. Let Iona decide whether to stay.',line:'You offer Ferren a chance to explain. Iona stays close enough to interrupt.',next:'ferren',effect:{trust:5},flag:'heardFerren',journal:'The Crown is searching for people whose imaginations change reality.'},
 {label:'Help Iona escape through a door that should not be there.',line:'A door appears in the painted brick. The Crown’s man lets you go, but memorizes your face.',next:'archive',effect:{magic:8,trust:6},flag:'withIona',journal:'Iona and I slipped away through a door I made.'},
 {label:'Offer Ferren a bargain: the truth for a chance to find his sister.',line:'His practiced smile disappears. “Her name is Lark,” he says. “The Crown says she never existed.”',next:'ferren',effect:{trust:8,resolve:3},flag:'larkPromise',journal:'Ferren is looking for his missing sister, Lark.'}
 ]},
 ferren:{act:'Chapter I · The impossible made intimate',place:'Bellweather · The rain archive',day:'Autumn · Day 3',art:'⌕',title:'A man filing the impossible',text:`Ferren takes you to the archive, where rain falls upward inside glass jars. He keeps his voice low. He joined the Ministry of Measure to find his sister Lark, a girl whose drawings could make small things real. The Ministry took her name from every register after she vanished.\n\nHe does not ask you to trust him. He asks you to look at the ledger he stole. Your parents’ names are there, crossed out in silver ink; beside them, a notation: “the first unbound.”`,speaker:'Mr. Ferren',quote:'“The Crown does not fear magic. It fears what it cannot count. Your parents made a world outside its ledger.”',quest:'The names in the silver ledger',qcopy:'Find the observatory where the Ministry kept the first ledger. Learn what happened to your parents—and to Lark.',qstep:'THREAD 03 · THE ARCHIVE BELOW',hint:'Imagine the ink loosening, or ask Ferren what he is willing to risk.',choices:[
 {label:'Trust Ferren with the letter. Let him read your parents’ words.',line:'He reads without touching the paper. When he is done, he looks less alone.',next:'archive',effect:{trust:10},flag:'trustedFerren',journal:'Ferren’s sister Lark could also make drawings real.'},
 {label:'Ask Iona what she knows about the first unbound.',line:'Iona turns one of her broken clocks over. Inside is a map, etched onto the spring.',next:'archive',effect:{trust:7,magic:4},flag:'ionaMap',journal:'Iona has a map to the Ministry’s underground archive.'},
 {label:'Refuse the ledger. Make your own way to the observatory.',line:'Ferren lets you go, though disappointment crosses his face. “Then find out for yourself,” he says.',next:'archive',effect:{resolve:7,magic:3},flag:'independent'}
 ]},
 archive:{act:'Chapter II · The things we keep',place:'The Ministry · Archive beneath the river',day:'Autumn · Day 5',art:'⌗',title:'A library with no shelves',text:`The old archive is below the river, in a chamber held dry by a promise no one remembers making. Its books hang in the air, chained by their spines to nothing. Names float like pale fish through the dark. Your parents’ ledger waits on a stone lectern.\n\nThe silver ink is a lock. It responds to a memory: a lullaby from the portrait, a smell of rain, a feeling you have not named yet. Iona steadies the lantern. Ferren stands watch at the stairs. For a moment, they are not opposing sides. They are two people choosing to stay.`,speaker:'A message in the margin',quote:'“If you have found this, we could not stay. We left the choice where you would find it.”',quest:'The truth beneath the river',qcopy:'Open the silver ledger. Choose what truth to carry into the world, and who gets to carry it with you.',qstep:'THREAD 03 · READ THE LEDGER',hint:'Imagine the page remembers your parents, or create a memory of your own.',choices:[
 {label:'Imagine your parents’ voices are still in the ink.',line:'The silver lifts into two bright threads. The ledger opens, and their last recorded memory blooms.',next:'ledger',effect:{magic:12,trust:4},flag:'parentsMessage',journal:'The archive remembers my parents choosing freedom over safety.'},
 {label:'Ask Iona and Ferren to open it with you.',line:'Three hands rest on the cover. The lock recognizes a choice made together.',next:'ledger',effect:{trust:10},flag:'together',journal:'Iona and Ferren chose to stay with me in the archive.'},
 {label:'Break the ledger open. You will not let it decide what is hidden.',line:'The lock cracks like winter ice. A pulse of silver light races up the river.',next:'ledger',effect:{resolve:8,magic:8},flag:'brokeLedger',journal:'I broke the Ministry’s silver lock and set its names free.'}
 ]},
 ledger:{act:'Chapter II · The things we keep',place:'The Ministry · Archive beneath the river',day:'Autumn · Day 5',art:'✧',title:'The story is not the same as the truth',text:`Your parents’ memory is not a neat answer. They built the hidden room as a refuge for people whose imaginations refused to be measured. When the Ministry came, they scattered the doors and hid the names. They did not die in the archive. They vanished beyond a door they made together—and never found a way back.\n\nThe ledger shows one more name: Lark. Not crossed out. Not erased. A trail of ink leads to the old observatory at the edge of the city, where the Ministry first learned to fold a place out of the world.`,speaker:'Iona',quote:'“A trail is not a promise. But it’s better than another blank page.”',quest:'The observatory at the edge',qcopy:'Reach the old observatory before the Ministry seals it. Find Lark, or find out what became of her.',qstep:'THREAD 04 · THE FAR SHORE',hint:'Imagine a way across the river that carries your companions, too.',choices:[
 {label:'Bring Iona and Ferren with you. No one gets left behind.',line:'Iona says yes before you finish asking. Ferren hesitates, then folds the ledger under his coat.',next:'river',effect:{trust:10},flag:'companions',journal:'My parents vanished through a door they made together.'},
 {label:'Ask Ferren to take the ledger to safety while you go ahead.',line:'He argues, then accepts. “I will find the door,” he says. “You find the person.”',next:'river',effect:{resolve:6,trust:4},flag:'ferrenAlone'},
 {label:'Follow the ink-trail alone, before anyone can stop you.',line:'The others let you go, though Iona presses a broken watch into your hand.',next:'river',effect:{resolve:8},flag:'alone'}
 ]},
 river:{act:'Chapter II · The things we keep',place:'The River of Unsaid Things',day:'Autumn · Day 6',art:'≈',title:'Crossing what was never said',text:`The river runs uphill into a sky without stars. Every ripple carries a sentence someone swallowed: I am sorry. I am afraid. Please stay. On the far shore, the observatory leans over the water like a question mark.\n\nA ferry waits. There is no ferryman, only a little girl’s drawing of a boat pinned to its bow. The drawing is fading. Your imagination could give it a shape, but it might ask something of you in return.`,speaker:'The river, which is a little like your own voice',quote:'“What you carry across is what you choose not to leave behind.”',quest:'Cross the River of Unsaid Things',qcopy:'Make the crossing. The thing you imagine may decide what the river asks of you.',qstep:'THREAD 04 · CROSS THE RIVER',hint:'Imagine a bridge, a boat, or a way for everyone to cross safely.',choices:[
 {label:'Give the drawing a boat made from a memory of home.',line:'The boat becomes real, blue as the pressed flower. The river asks for a memory in exchange; you give it one small, warm thing.',next:'observatory',effect:{magic:9,resolve:-2},flag:'memoryBoat',journal:'I gave the river a memory to bring my friends across.'},
 {label:'Imagine a bridge so every traveler can cross together.',line:'A bridge of pale paper unfurls over the water. It holds because everyone steps onto it at once.',next:'observatory',effect:{magic:12,trust:5},flag:'bridge',journal:'I made a bridge wide enough for all of us.'},
 {label:'Ask the river what it wants, and listen before making anything.',line:'The river answers in your mother’s lullaby. It wants a name for the child who drew the boat.',next:'observatory',effect:{trust:8,magic:6},flag:'riverName',journal:'Listening can be a kind of magic.'}
 ]},
 observatory:{act:'Chapter III · A door without a lock',place:'The old observatory · The far shore',day:'Autumn · Day 7',art:'☾',title:'A door at the end of the map',text:`The observatory’s brass dome is split open to the weather. Inside, stars turn beneath the floor. At the center of the chamber stands a door made from the same dark wood as the portrait frame. It has no handle.\n\nA figure waits beside it: Lark, older than the little girl in Ferren’s memory, with ink on her fingers and a watch stopped at the wrong hour. Mr. Ferren says her name. She looks at him as if she has been holding that name in her mouth for years. Behind them, the Crown’s Warden arrives with a quiet squad and a ledger of his own.`,speaker:'Lark',quote:'“I made this place to hide in. I forgot how to make a way out.”',quest:'The door your parents made',qcopy:'Decide what the door should do. The Warden wants to seal it; Lark wants to open it; your parents may be beyond it.',qstep:'THREAD 05 · CHOOSE WHAT COMES NEXT',hint:'Imagine a door that offers a choice instead of taking one away.',choices:[
 {label:'Go to Ferren and Lark. Let them have the first word.',line:'The siblings reach for each other, then stop a breath apart. Neither of them knows what comes after being found.',next:'warden',effect:{trust:11},flag:'reunited',journal:'Ferren and Lark found each other again.'},
 {label:'Stand between the Warden and the door. Ask why he is afraid.',line:'You ask him a human question. For one heartbeat, the Warden has no answer ready.',next:'warden',effect:{resolve:8,trust:3},flag:'questionedWarden'},
 {label:'Imagine the door opening only for those who choose to enter.',line:'The wood glows at its edges. A new seam appears: not a lock, but an invitation.',next:'warden',effect:{magic:12},flag:'choiceDoor',journal:'I imagined a door that could only be entered by choice.'}
 ]},
 warden:{act:'Chapter III · A door without a lock',place:'The old observatory · The far shore',day:'Autumn · Day 7',art:'♜',title:'The Warden’s arithmetic',text:`Warden Sable lays down his ledger. It contains the names of everyone the Ministry has ever tried to make legible: makers, dreamers, people who would not stay inside their assigned stories. He tells you that the Crown was built after a city nearly drowned in unbounded magic. His fear is not invented. Neither is the harm he has done with it.\n\n“Give me the door,” he says. “Let me make sure no one can lose the world again.” The door waits. So do Iona, Ferren, and Lark. They are watching you, but none of them has asked you to decide for them.`,speaker:'Warden Sable',quote:'“You can imagine anything. Can you imagine a limit you would choose?”',quest:'What a free world asks of us',qcopy:'The door can restore, release, or remake. Choose the world you can live with—or invent another.',qstep:'THREAD 05 · THE LAST PAGE',hint:'Your imagination can make a fourth choice. What future do you want everyone to be able to choose?',choices:[
 {label:'Open the door. Let the missing people decide if they want to return.',line:'You ask the door to become an invitation. No one is pulled through. No one is kept out.',next:'finaleOpen',effect:{magic:9,trust:7},flag:'openDoor',journal:'I made the door an invitation, not an order.'},
 {label:'Close the door, but free every name in the Crown’s ledger.',line:'The door settles into the wood. The names rise from every Ministry page and fly into the night.',next:'finaleFree',effect:{resolve:9,trust:5},flag:'freeNames',journal:'I freed the names in the ledger without forcing the door open.'},
 {label:'Remake the rules: make every impossible thing answer to its maker.',line:'You picture a world where magic is shared, accountable, and never held by one office. The observatory listens.',next:'finaleRewrite',effect:{magic:13,resolve:4},flag:'newRules',journal:'I imagined new rules for a world that belongs to everyone.'}
 ]},
 finaleOpen:{act:'Epilogue · The page remains yours',place:'The threshold · Somewhere between',day:'A new beginning',art:'✧',title:'An invitation, at last',text:`The door opens on a sunlit room full of people who have been missing from the world. Some step through. Some smile and stay where they are. At the back of the room, two familiar strangers turn toward you. Your mother’s laugh reaches you first. Your father is holding a paper bird.\n\nThey are not the same as a memory. Neither are you. There is time, now, to learn each other slowly. Iona begins a school for unmeasured things. Ferren leaves the Ministry and helps Lark build a life that belongs to her. Warden Sable stays to answer for what he did—and to help dismantle the ledger.`,speaker:'Your mother',quote:'“We left you a beginning. Look what you made of it.”',quest:'The story keeps going',qcopy:'Your choices made a world with open doors and no forced return. Start a new story to discover a different path.',qstep:'EPILOGUE · A DOOR LEFT OPEN',hint:'Imagine a new first page. Every new story changes the details.',ending:'Open the door. You made a future where the lost could choose to come home.',choices:[{label:'Keep this story and begin again',line:'A new blank page waits. The world will take a different shape.',next:'letter',newRun:true}]},
 finaleFree:{act:'Epilogue · The page remains yours',place:'Bellweather · A city of unbound names',day:'A new beginning',art:'❋',title:'The names took flight',text:`At dawn, the ledger’s names are everywhere: stitched into coat linings, sung by fish in the canal, written in the frost on the observatory glass. The door closes, but the people it hid are not erased; they have a way to be found now, when they choose.\n\nYour parents remain beyond the threshold, their fate uncertain—but the Crown can no longer make anyone disappear on paper. Iona and Lark fill the market with clocks that tell the truth. Ferren writes a new record: one that leaves room for people to change.`,speaker:'Ferren',quote:'“A name is not a cage if the person gets to carry it.”',quest:'The story keeps going',qcopy:'Your choices broke the Crown’s monopoly on memory. Start a new story to discover a different path.',qstep:'EPILOGUE · NAMES SET FREE',hint:'Imagine a new first page. Every new story changes the details.',ending:'You freed every name. The door stays closed, but nobody is forgotten again.',choices:[{label:'Keep this story and begin again',line:'A new blank page waits. The world will take a different shape.',next:'letter',newRun:true}]},
 finaleRewrite:{act:'Epilogue · The page remains yours',place:'The observatory · A world in revision',day:'A new beginning',art:'✺',title:'The world, rewritten together',text:`The magic does not become tame. It becomes answerable. Across Bellweather, people begin making small impossible things together: a bridge that asks before it carries you, a clinic that grows what its patients need, a clock that gives back one hour to anyone who has lost one.\n\nYour parents’ door becomes a meeting place. They come through when they are ready, and leave again when they need to. Warden Sable gives up his office. Iona, Lark, and Ferren help write the new covenant, and leave the last page blank on purpose.`,speaker:'Lark',quote:'“You did not fix the world. You gave it room to keep fixing itself.”',quest:'The story keeps going',qcopy:'Your imagination changed the rules—and left room for everyone else. Start a new story to discover a different path.',qstep:'EPILOGUE · THE WORLD IN REVISION',hint:'Imagine a new first page. Every new story changes the details.',ending:'You rewrote the rules with everyone, and left the last page open.',choices:[{label:'Keep this story and begin again',line:'A new blank page waits. The world will take a different shape.',next:'letter',newRun:true}]}
};
const SAVE_KEY='ink-and-elsewhere-save-v1';
const freshState=()=>({scene:'letter',name:'The Unwritten',magic:18,resolve:50,trust:32,day:1,turn:1,flags:{},journal:[],feed:['A blank page, a held breath'],after:'',customCount:0,run:1});
let state=loadState()||freshState();
function loadState(){try{const raw=localStorage.getItem(SAVE_KEY);if(!raw)return null;const parsed=JSON.parse(raw);return parsed&&scenes[parsed.scene]?parsed:null}catch{return null}}
function persistQuiet(){try{localStorage.setItem(SAVE_KEY,JSON.stringify(state))}catch{}}
function persist(){persistQuiet();toast('Story saved in this browser.')}
function clamp(n){return Math.max(0,Math.min(100,n))}
function escapeHTML(s){return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','"':'&quot;',"'":'&#39;'}[c]))}
function toast(message){const el=document.getElementById('toast');el.textContent=message;el.classList.add('show');clearTimeout(toast.timer);toast.timer=setTimeout(()=>el.classList.remove('show'),2100)}
function addJournal(entry){if(!entry||state.journal.includes(entry))return;state.journal.unshift(entry);state.journal=state.journal.slice(0,5)}
function addFeed(text){state.feed.unshift(text);state.feed=state.feed.slice(0,4)}
function setMeter(id,value){document.getElementById(id+'Val').textContent=`${value} / 100`;document.getElementById(id+'Bar').style.width=`${value}%`}
function render(){const s=scenes[state.scene];if(!s){state=freshState();return render()}document.getElementById('playerName').textContent=state.name||'The Unwritten';document.getElementById('playerSub').textContent=state.flags.awakened?'Maker of impossible things · Unbound':'Orphan · Unawakened';setMeter('magic',state.magic);setMeter('resolve',state.resolve);setMeter('trust',state.trust);document.getElementById('questTitle').textContent=s.quest;document.getElementById('questCopy').textContent=s.qcopy;document.getElementById('questStep').textContent=s.qstep;document.getElementById('journalCount').textContent=String(state.journal.length).padStart(2,'0');document.getElementById('journalList').innerHTML=state.journal.length?state.journal.map(x=>`<div class="journal-entry">${escapeHTML(x)}</div>`).join(''):'<div class="journal-entry">The page is waiting for its first truth.</div>';document.getElementById('location').textContent=s.place;document.getElementById('day').textContent=s.day;document.getElementById('chapterLabel').textContent=s.act;document.getElementById('sceneArt').textContent=s.art;document.getElementById('sceneTitle').textContent=s.title;const prose=document.getElementById('prose');prose.textContent=s.text;prose.style.whiteSpace='pre-line';if(state.after){const p=document.createElement('p');p.style.cssText='color:#e0c891;margin-top:18px;border-left:1px solid #aa8e5a;padding-left:14px';p.textContent=state.after;prose.appendChild(p)}const dialogue=document.getElementById('dialogue');dialogue.innerHTML=s.speaker?`<div class="scene-divider"></div><div class="speaker">${escapeHTML(s.speaker)}</div><div class="quote">“${escapeHTML(s.quote)}”</div>`:'';const ending=document.getElementById('ending');ending.innerHTML=s.ending?`<div class="ending-panel"><h3>The end—for now</h3><p>${escapeHTML(s.ending)}</p></div>`:'';document.getElementById('choices').innerHTML=s.choices.map((c,i)=>`<button class="choice" data-index="${i+1}" data-choice="${i}">${escapeHTML(c.label)}</button>`).join('');document.querySelectorAll('[data-choice]').forEach(btn=>btn.addEventListener('click',()=>choose(Number(btn.dataset.choice))));document.getElementById('hint').textContent=s.hint;document.getElementById('turnLabel').textContent=`TURN ${String(state.turn).padStart(2,'0')}`;document.getElementById('feedLines').innerHTML=state.feed.map((x,i)=>`<span class="feed-chip ${i>2?'muted':''}"><b>${i===0?'NOW':'THEN'}</b> · ${escapeHTML(x)}</span>`).join('');document.getElementById('createBox').style.display=s.ending?'none':'block';document.getElementById('imagineInput').placeholder=state.magic<8?'Your imagination needs a quiet moment…':'I imagine that…';document.getElementById('imagineInput').disabled=state.magic<8;document.querySelector('.manifest-btn').disabled=state.magic<8;document.querySelector('.manifest-btn').style.opacity=state.magic<8?'.5':'1'}
function choose(index){const s=scenes[state.scene],c=s.choices[index];if(!c)return;for(const [key,value] of Object.entries(c.effect||{}))state[key]=clamp(state[key]+value);if(c.flag)state.flags[c.flag]=true;if(c.journal)addJournal(c.journal);if(state.scene==='awakening')state.flags.awakened=true;state.after=c.line;addFeed(c.label);state.turn++;if(c.newRun){state.run++;state.scene='letter';state.magic=18;state.resolve=50;state.trust=32;state.day=1;state.turn=1;state.flags={};state.journal=[];state.feed=['A blank page, a held breath'];state.after='A new story begins. The same city is waiting, but it does not remember the same future.';state.customCount=0}else{state.scene=c.next;if(c.next==='letterOpen')state.day=1;else if(c.next==='laundry')state.day=2;else if(c.next==='city'||c.next==='marketChoice'||c.next==='ferren')state.day=3;else if(c.next==='archive')state.day=5;else if(c.next==='river')state.day=6;else if(c.next==='observatory'||c.next==='warden')state.day=7;else if(c.next.startsWith('finale'))state.day=8}persistQuiet();render();window.scrollTo({top:0,behavior:'smooth'})}
const visions={
 door:['The wall accepts the thought, then reshapes it: not quite a door, more a promise that there is another side.','A seam of warm light appears where none belonged. Something on the other side knocks once, politely.','The idea takes hold. The world makes room for a way through, though it leaves the choice of crossing to you.'],
 friend:['Your imagined kindness becomes a small, practical thing. Someone notices—and chooses to stay beside you.','The world gives the thought a face: a familiar hand, offered without asking for anything back.','A quiet warmth passes between you and the people nearby. It is not a spell anyone can own.'],
 flight:['The room fills with a soft rush of wings. Your creation circles once, then points toward the next question.','The thing you imagined catches the air and carries a scrap of possibility across the room.','A little impossible creature takes shape, bright-eyed and temporary. It seems pleased to be here.'],
 shelter:['A shelter takes shape around the people you want to protect. It holds, not because it is unbreakable, but because you made it together.','You imagine a safe place. The air gentles; the nearest frightened person finally lets out a breath.','The world bends into a small refuge, stitched from whatever is close at hand.'],
 memory:['A memory you did not know you had turns up at the edge of the thought: rain, a lullaby, a hand in yours.','For a moment, the past is not a locked room. It is a window you can choose to look through.','The air takes on the scent of a remembered place. It does not answer every question, but it answers this one.'],
 wonder:['The idea refuses to stay a simple idea. It gathers a little light and becomes its own curious, imperfect thing.','Reality considers your proposal, then adds a detail you never thought of: a small brass bell, ringing underwater.','The imagined thing appears, not exactly as requested. It has its own character now, and that makes it feel more real.']
};
function imagine(raw){const idea=raw.trim();if(!idea)return;const lower=idea.toLowerCase(),s=scenes[state.scene];const category=/door|gate|key|open|portal|wall|passage/.test(lower)?'door':/friend|help|trust|together|listen|share|hold|comfort|protect|save/.test(lower)?'friend':/bird|fly|wing|air|cloud|light/.test(lower)?'flight':/home|safe|shelter|shield|warm|hide|refuge/.test(lower)?'shelter':/remember|memory|past|parent|mother|father|lullaby|name/.test(lower)?'memory':'wonder';const outcomes=visions[category];const seed=(idea.length+state.turn*7+state.run*11)%outcomes.length;let effect=4+Math.min(8,Math.floor(idea.length/18))+Math.floor(Math.random()*4);if(category==='friend'||/iona|ferren|lark|vale|sable/.test(lower)){state.trust=clamp(state.trust+4);effect+=1}state.magic=clamp(state.magic+effect);if(/brave|risk|stand|refuse|fight|face/.test(lower))state.resolve=clamp(state.resolve+3);state.customCount++;state.turn++;let reply=outcomes[seed];if(state.scene==='letter'||state.scene==='letterOpen')reply+=' The brass key turns slightly toward the old laundry stairs.';else if(state.scene==='laundry')reply+=' The hidden room answers with a ripple of starlight.';else if(state.scene==='awakening')reply+=' Your parents’ portrait watches without trying to steer you.';else if(state.scene==='city'||state.scene==='marketChoice'||state.scene==='ferren')reply+=' Iona glances at what you made; Ferren quietly writes down what it might mean.';else if(state.scene==='archive'||state.scene==='ledger')reply+=' A few names drift free of the silver ink and circle your hand.';else if(state.scene==='river')reply+=' The current softens, carrying the thought toward the far shore.';else if(state.scene==='observatory'||state.scene==='warden')reply+=' The door listens, but does not open for anyone who has not chosen it.';state.after=`You imagine: “${idea}” ${reply}`;addFeed(`Imagined: ${idea.length>34?idea.slice(0,31)+'…':idea}`);if(state.customCount===1)addJournal('I can give the world shape by imagining something real.');if(state.customCount===3)addJournal('My power grows when I give it a purpose.');persistQuiet();render();document.getElementById('imagineInput').value='';document.getElementById('imagineInput').focus()}
document.getElementById('imagineForm').addEventListener('submit',e=>{e.preventDefault();imagine(document.getElementById('imagineInput').value)});
document.getElementById('saveBtn').addEventListener('click',persist);
document.getElementById('newBtn').addEventListener('click',()=>document.getElementById('modal').classList.add('open'));
document.getElementById('modalCancel').addEventListener('click',()=>document.getElementById('modal').classList.remove('open'));
document.getElementById('modalConfirm').addEventListener('click',()=>{state=freshState();state.run=(Number(loadState()?.run)||0)+1;state.after='A new story begins. The same city is waiting, but it does not remember the same future.';persistQuiet();render();document.getElementById('modal').classList.remove('open');toast('A new story begins.')});
document.getElementById('modal').addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target.id==='modal')e.currentTarget.classList.remove('open')});
document.getElementById('playerName').addEventListener('click',()=>{const name=prompt('What name do you want this story to call you?',state.name==='The Unwritten'?'':state.name);if(name&&name.trim()){state.name=name.trim().slice(0,28);persistQuiet();render()}});
document.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{if(e.key==='Escape')document.getElementById('modal').classList.remove('open');if((e.key==='s'||e.key==='S')&&(e.ctrlKey||e.metaKey)){e.preventDefault();persist()}});
render();persistQuiet();
</script>
</body>
